      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The debate isn't about whether safeguards *can* be implemented; it's about whether they are *sufficient* to prevent mission creep and overreach by powerful surveillance apparatuses. Proponents of unchecked technological deployment often downplay the inherent power imbalance created when the state can track every citizen in real-time. Therefore, even with perfect legal frameworks, the fundamental shift toward pervasive surveillance fundamentally alters the relationship between the citizen and the state, which is a non-negotiable political issue.",
      "source": "target",
